00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.189 align:start position:0%
 
with call of duty modern warfare  Infinity Ward is taking every aspect of  the call of duty multiplayer formula and  re-evaluating it the developer gave us a  chance to place several multiplayer game  modes at its reveal event where Infinity  Ward's showed off the changes it's  making to the way you'll compete in the  game in many ways modern warfare is  dialing back to an earlier part in the  franchise's history while rethinking a  lot of the elements along the way the  thing that will probably affect the way  most players approach modern warfare is  the map design Infinity Ward is moving  away from the three lane map style  that's prevalent in a lot of shooters  and in many recent Cod games those maps  have three general paths from one end to  the other and most of the time your  major tactical decisions hinge on which  route you take toward the enemy Modern  Warfare's Maps instead are much more  like real urban areas and mostly rely on  freestanding buildings to create  locations for player engagements it's  all about positioning buildings create  power positions where you can get better  vantage points and sight lines than your  enemies a big focus is on climbing  objects and mantling allowing you to  find different paths to high points or  out-of-the-way places being able to  climb up into windows or over ruined  walls also gives you opportunities to  flank out enemies who are taking out  your teammates from those power  positions too another big addition doors  modern warfare adds doors that you can  open and close creating and closing off  sight lines and player paths using doors  strategically is also very important to  winning fights open a door while you're  aiming down the sights of your gun and  you'll push it open just a bit and peek  in giving you a chance to toss in a  flashbang or take a few shots at  unsuspecting players you can also run or  slide through doors and kick them open  with a melee attack or breach them with  any explosive in the game for a much  louder approach you're also going to  want to use doors to get information on  enemies the sound of doors open and can  give you clues when people are sneaking  up on you Modern Warfare does away with  personal radar in most circumstances so  you're going to need that Intel part of  the point of Infinity Ward's rework of  cult Duty multiplayer is supporting a  variety of play styles the map design is  part of that support as is the new  gunsmith system it takes loadout  customization much farther allowing you  to kit out every one of your guns to  your specification even in the midst of  battle gun support a variety of tats  from barrels to sites to stocks and  triggers as in past Call of Duty games  you'll unlock gun pieces as you play  anywhere between thirty and sixty for  every gun pistols have fewer because  they're smaller  whole rifles have many more you can add  five attachments to any gun which have  benefits and drawbacks a scope will  increase an assault rifles range for  instance while making it heavier and  therefore a bit slower to pull up for  aiming down sights you can also add a  perk to a gun in lieu of one attachment  which offers things like fast or melee  attacks or better bullet penetration  also supporting new play styles are the  return of killstreaks first of all  that's a change from previous games in  the franchise that used scorestreaks  those are rewards of special weapons or  abilities that were based on how many  kills you notched but also on things  like taking objectives or other means of  accumulating points  Modern Warfare switches back to kill  streaks to make earning those bonuses a  little more predictable but it also is  making them a bit more diverse  for example modern warfare gets rid of  your traditional personal radar and  mini-map where in previous games you  could see the locations of other players  whenever they fire their weapons now  you'll need a kill streak to launch a  personal radar helicopter or a UAV drone  to get that information other kill  streaks let you call in drivable  vehicles like tanks that other players  can climb aboard yep vehicles are going  to be a big part of modern warfare  modern warfare also gives you support  opportunities with a new item in your  equipment loadout these items fall into  a category called field upgrades and run  on cooldown timers they include things  like a small recon drone that can fly  around and mark targets for you or ammo  boxes that you can drop to help resupply  your team a big tenant Infinity Ward  keeps mentioning when they talk about  modern warfare is unifying the  experience across all the game modes  right now call of duty often feels like  three games packaged together a  single-player campaign a multiplayer  game and a co-op game like zombies  modern warfare still has all three  although it switches out zombies for the  original Modern Warfare's SpecOps mode  but they should feel more similar to one  another the guns you use in  single-player will handle the same way  they do in multiplayer and your  progression with weapons and spec ops  will carry over to multiplayer we also  got to try out the new cross play  capabilities of modern warfare at the  event which were pretty seamless we  raise the question of whether Infinity  Ward expects PC players to wallop their  console counterparts and matches but  according to the developers that hasn't  been much of a problem  the real determining factor is  individual skill on a given platform  even still Infinity Ward told us their  work  features behind-the-scenes in modern  warfare to make sure everyone gets a  fair shake no matter what platform  they're playing on during our hands-on  time with Modern Warfare's multiplayer  we found all the changes that Infinity  Ward is making felt really strong though  a lot of them are channeling call of  duty of years past they feel like a big  refresher for the franchise's formula  they also help it stand out among a  growing field of first-person shooters  at least after a few hours of playtime  with its focus on new technology cross  play and revisiting and refining old  aspects of the franchise it seems like  Infinity Ward has accomplished that goal  and like modern warfare could be a big  step forward for Call of Duty  you

